<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mayurasharma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · Also known as Mayuravarma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mayurasharma was the founder of the Kadamba dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> in the mid-4th century CE. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talagunda-inscription">Talagunda inscription</a>, he was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> scholar who, insulted by a Pallava horseman at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>, took up arms, defeated the Pallava frontier forces and forced them to recognise his rule. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banavasi">Banavasi</a> his capital and is regarded as the founder of the first native <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mayurasharma.jpg" alt="Mayurasharma" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bengaluru Inscriptions Digital Conservation Team · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Talagunda_Pillar_Inscription1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
